      en: "Sembel is an archaeological site near Asmara, Eritrea, containing remains of a pre-Aksumite city from the 7th to 5th centuries BCE. Discovered in the 1990s, it provides evidence of early urban civilization in the region. Finds include pottery, building foundations, and tombs. Sembel is considered one of the oldest settlements in the Horn of Africa. It offers crucial insights into pre-Aksumite culture and trade. Excavations are carried out by Italian and Eritrean archaeologists.",
