      en: "The Halhal battlefield, near Mendefera in the Debub region, was the site of a pivotal engagement in the Eritrean War of Independence on May 23, 1988. The EPLF forces decisively defeated the Ethiopian army, breaking the siege of Asmara and shifting the war's momentum. The rugged terrain still bears evidence of the conflict, with trenches and rusting military hardware. A memorial honors the fallen. The victory is considered a major step toward Eritrean independence, achieved in 1993.",
