      en: "Toka Eba is an archaeological site in the Gash-Barka region of western Eritrea, near the Ethiopian border. It is a pre-Aksumite settlement dating from the 1st millennium BCE, featuring remains of stone structures and tombs. The site has not been fully excavated but provides valuable insights into early habitation of the Eritrean highlands. Toka Eba is of significant research interest. The surrounding area is semi-arid, used for pastoralism.",
